# Repository-wide line-ending policy.
#
# Git for Windows sets `core.autocrlf=true` in the system config, which converts
# LF -> CRLF on checkout and prints warnings like:
#   "warning: in the working copy of 'x.jsx', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next
#    time Git touches it"
# Pinning `eol=lf` here overrides core.autocrlf for every matched path, so the
# repository stays normalized to LF (as it already is) and the warnings stop.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts must keep CRLF to execute correctly.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets - never convert or diff these as text.
*.pdf binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
